<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Consulate of the Sea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Llibre del Consolat de Mar, Consolat de Mar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Consolat de Mar is a collection of maritime customs and laws compiled in Catalan, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> in the fourteenth century, and printed in 1484. Used by the sea consulates of the Crown of Aragon, it covered shipping, trade and prize law and was widely followed across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/consulate-of-the-sea.jpg" alt="Consulate of the Sea" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kent Wang from Barcelona, Spain · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Llotja_de_la_Seda_(52042949244).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
